1
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:12,080
=Fatal Proximity to Him=

2
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:14,120
=Episode 19=

3
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,800
I'd offer my life...

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,520
to bring Xiyu back.

5
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:43,960
♪I hide my racing heart without a sound♪

6
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:50,520
♪I close my eyes and pretend
the story's been reset♪

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,640
♪I steer clear of every path
that leads to you♪

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,800
♪Trying to outrun the storm
we're destined for♪

9
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:00,720
♪I thought if I didn't hear, see,
or speak of you♪

10
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:01,360
He Lan?

11
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:03,040
He Lan!

12
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:07,280
He Lan, wake up!

13
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:10,440
Wake up! I won't let you die!

14
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:11,880
He Lan, wake up!

15
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:15,520
♪In this new cycle, I watch you
become innocent again♪

16
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:16,680
(I'd offer my life)

17
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:18,360
(to bring you back.)

18
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:20,200
(I'd offer my life)

19
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:21,880
(to bring you back.)

20
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:23,560
(I'd offer my life)

21
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:25,120
(to bring you back.)

22
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:29,880
Did He Lan die for me nine times?

23
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:32,760
Every time I was murdered,

24
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:35,280
He Lan made a wish on the ring.

25
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:37,000
He chose to die in my place.

26
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:38,880
(I'd offer my life)

27
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:42,440
(to bring Xiyu back.)

28
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:47,880
♪Maybe if I retreat to the edge
of my dreams♪

29
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:50,920
♪I could give you another future♪

30
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:53,520
♪A tomorrow where I no longer exist♪

31
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:54,320
Not saying anything?

32
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,520
Then I must be right.

33
00:01:57,920 --> 00:02:00,240
I became self-aware during
the sixth loop.

34
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:02,960
But without the ring's power

35
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:04,760
keeping me alive,

36
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:06,160
I would've died long ago.

37
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:08,480
You're above life and death.

38
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:10,880
From the very beginning,

39
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:12,200
you've been like someone
in the audience,

40
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,400
watching us perform.

41
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:16,400
Zhang Jinghang killed me
again and again,

42
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:17,360
and you didn't stop him.

43
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,680
He Lan died for me again and again,

44
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,920
and you didn't stop that either.

45
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:23,800
You must find this
endless cycle of death

46
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:24,520
hilarious, don't you?

47
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:28,640
(Your darn love)

48
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:30,680
(has caused me enough trouble already.)

49
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:32,800
(If I could stop He Lan,)

50
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:35,240
(I would've met my KPI ages ago.)

51
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:38,200
So even you can't do anything?

52
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,240
(No.)

53
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:45,480
Then why does Zhang Jinghang
keep killing me?

54
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,480
Answer me.

55
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:52,000
Answer me!

56
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:55,800
(That's the truth you're supposed
to uncover.)

57
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,720
(How would I know?)

58
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:00,760
(Emergency)

59
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:04,000
Mom.

60
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,040
How did it go?

61
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:08,960
The doctor said

62
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,000
I'm recovering pretty well.

63
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:11,720
Your leg

64
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,080
has only just started getting better.

65
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:15,040
You have to be extra careful at school.

66
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:17,320
Senior year is hard enough as it is.

67
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:18,600
Get yourself healthy,

68
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:19,600
catch up on your studies,

69
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:20,880
and get into Tsinghua
or Peking University.

70
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,800
Then with one of my biggest wishes
coming true, I can finally rest easy.

71
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:23,640
Mom,

72
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:24,600
um...

73
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:27,120
is my classmate's mother still here?

74
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,040
The one who just had surgery
for a perforated stomach?

75
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:30,120
You mean

76
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:31,640
your class monitor, Zhang...

77
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:32,360
Zhang Jinghang.

78
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,240
Right, that's him.

79
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:34,600
His mother

80
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:36,000
is recovering pretty well
after the surgery.

81
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:37,640
The main problem is that

82
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:39,120
the perforation was caused by

83
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:39,880
her hepatitis C,

84
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:41,040
so she's very weak.

85
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:43,120
Luckily, her family's taking
great care of her.

86
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:44,080
You mean...

87
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:45,440
Zhang Jinghang's dad?

88
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:46,000
Yeah.

89
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,880
I can tell he's dependable.

90
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:49,600
He has a caregiver watch her
during the day,

91
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:51,600
then stays with her himself
at night and on weekends.

92
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:53,200
And he's taking care of his son
in his senior year too.

93
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:54,920
If your dad

94
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,840
had been half as caring and responsible,

95
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:57,520
back then,

96
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,800
I wouldn't have divorced him.

97
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:01,040
He never took any responsibility
as a husband or father.

98
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:01,560
Exactly.

99
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,440
He cheated on you right after
I was born.

100
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,840
And that gold lock he gave me
for my one-month celebration

101
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:06,040
was gold-plated silver.

102
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:06,400
What?

103
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:07,200
Gold-plated silver?

104
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:09,400
What kind of father does that?

105
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:11,080
I'm calling him about this.

106
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:12,440
Yeah, call him and give him hell.

107
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:13,320
I'm leaving.

108
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:19,600
How'd it go?

109
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:20,200
Done.

110
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:20,800
Let's go.

111
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:23,000
(Emergency Surgery Clinic)

112
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:24,480
Does it hurt?

113
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:26,080
No.

114
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:27,520
How about here?

115
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:28,520
Oh, you.

116
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:32,440
Son,

117
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:33,440
you went through a lot.

118
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:34,880
Here's one for you first.

119
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:36,120
Yeah.

120
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:36,960
You've earned it.

121
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:38,400
Give Mom one too.

122
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:39,960
Of course.

123
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:40,200
Here.

124
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:40,720
This one's for you.

125
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:46,400
I know why Zhang Jinghang hates me.

126
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:47,640
Why?

127
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:51,160
You have it.

128
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:53,360
Jichuan,

129
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:54,760
come outside with me.

130
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:56,760
Let's go.

131
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:58,960
It's okay.

132
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:00,280
You guys

133
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:00,920
wait here.

134
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:06,880
Zhang Jichuan, you scumbag!

135
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,360
You owe me an explanation!

136
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:09,320
Let go of me!

137
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:10,640
What do I have to explain?

138
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:12,640
Your son's alive and healthy,

139
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:13,800
while my daughter is lying in bed,

140
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:15,040
wishing she were dead!

141
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:15,840
Calm down.

142
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:16,920
Let's figure out what went wrong,

143
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:17,360
okay?

144
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,960
I trusted you!

145
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,240
She took your medicine,

146
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:21,120
and now my daughter...

147
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:22,240
her kidneys have failed,

148
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:23,200
and so has her liver!

149
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:24,360
Now

150
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:26,320
she needs dialysis just to stay alive.

151
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,320
She's getting worse every day!

152
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:29,760
If it caused a problem
for your daughter,

153
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:31,160
why was everyone else who took it fine?

154
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,320
You know nothing!

155
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:33,320
Two girls

156
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:34,360
took your medicine,

157
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:35,200
went into kidney failure,

158
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:35,880
and died!

159
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,240
And you're still making excuses?

160
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:38,480
I'll kill you!

161
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:42,360
My dad was just an employee
at an import-export company.

162
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:43,760
He only made the medicine
to treat my mom.

163
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:45,520
You came begging him for it.

164
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:46,720
That's the only reason
he gave it to you.

165
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:47,720
My mom took it too.

166
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:49,080
If there were something wrong with it,
how come she's fine?

167
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:50,280
And another thing.

168
00:06:50,760 --> 00:06:52,960
Your daughter took my dad's medicine
for a long time.

169
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:53,960
They were all fine before.

170
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:54,800
So how come

171
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:56,480
several patients suddenly got sick
at the same time?

172
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,080
Who gave you those pills?

173
00:06:58,520 --> 00:06:59,520
That blond guy!

174
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,320
He kept asking us for money

175
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:02,800
and tried to hurt us.

176
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:03,880
You know that blond guy too!

177
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:04,840
Blond guy?

178
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:05,360
Who?

179
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:09,200
So the cytidine Li Junsheng stole

180
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:09,960
from Wang Haotian's family's factory

181
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:11,480
was used to make sofosbuvir.

182
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,280
Sofosbuvir

183
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:15,080
is a highly effective drug
for treating hepatitis C.

184
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:16,480
Li Junsheng wanted to make money,

185
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,280
so he used substandard ingredients

186
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:18,800
and hurt a lot of people.

187
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:21,120
So Li Junsheng was the real culprit.

188
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:23,040
Because you reported Li Junsheng,

189
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:24,760
Zhang Jichuan got dragged into it.

190
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:25,960
He had no choice
but to flee the country.

191
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:28,160
When Zhang Jinghang's mom died,

192
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:28,920
(In Memoriam)
he tried to come back,

193
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:30,080
but died at sea.

194
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:31,880
("Justice" found in the South China Sea)
Zhang Jinghang said he hated you.

195
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:34,400
But why would he kill me
just because he hates you?

196
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:36,040
To get back at you?

197
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:40,320
That's probably most of the reason.

198
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:42,960
Then what's the other reason?

199
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,800
Because he likes you too.

200
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:49,040
If he can't have you, no one can.

201
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,040
Where did you get all that money?

202
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:01,560
I didn't steal or rob anyone.

203
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:08,520
(Love Sports; Choose ANTA)

204
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:09,040
Mom!

205
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:10,520
Mom, come here for a second!

206
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:11,600
Coming!

207
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,080
You two brothers

208
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:15,800
having a chat?

209
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:21,600
My boy!

210
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:22,960
It's all yours.

211
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:23,920
Spend it however you want!

212
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:25,600
My dearest boy,

213
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:26,440
you're amazing!

214
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:28,400
What did I tell you?

215
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,680
Good grades don't necessarily mean

216
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:31,480
you'll make good money

217
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,680
and take care of your parents.

218
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:34,040
You're so right.

219
00:08:36,040 --> 00:08:38,000
So you're supporting your parents
with blood money?

220
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,000
Why can't you ever stand

221
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:41,920
to see Junsheng doing well?

222
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:44,480
I know you're making fake drugs.

223
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:47,520
You wore my clothes and broke
into Wang Haotian's family's place,

224
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:49,080
then stole cytidine
to make generic drugs.

225
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,080
You injured Wang Haotian,

226
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:52,840
then framed me for it.

227
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:55,520
Even now, your mom
and my dad still think

228
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:56,880
I did all those things.

229
00:08:58,160 --> 00:08:59,480
Other people make medicine
to save lives.

230
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,720
Your fake drugs

231
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,480
are killing people. Don't you get it?

232
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:04,760
Are you crazy?

233
00:09:04,760 --> 00:09:05,760
What are you talking about?

234
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:08,400
I filmed the whole process
of you making those fake drugs.

235
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,040
I won't let you hurt anyone else.

236
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,640
What video?

237
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:14,360
What are you talking about?

238
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:15,440
What a psycho.

239
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:20,040
The abandoned cement factory.

240
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:28,840
He Lan.

241
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:29,880
He...

242
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:30,720
He Lan, I was wrong.

243
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:31,760
I admit it.

244
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:34,480
I shouldn't have framed you
for what happened to Wang Haotian.

245
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:35,760
But...

246
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:36,320
But...

247
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:38,440
Making fake drugs is no joke.

248
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:40,560
I could go to prison for that!

249
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:42,920
Give me the video.

250
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:43,480
Come on.

251
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,080
He Lan!

252
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,320
I'll cut you in.

253
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:47,760
We can make a fortune together.

254
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:50,760
You heard all that, right?

255
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:53,440
Who are you on the phone with?

256
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:56,560
(Officer Sha)

257
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:57,160
What?

258
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:58,200
A cop?

259
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:08,920
Last time, we got to
the funeral hall first.

260
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,560
Li Junsheng showed up right after us.

261
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:12,320
He must've followed our car.

262
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:14,040
No one's following us this time.

263
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:14,680
So,

264
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,880
why are we going so early?

265
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,680
The sooner we pay our respects,
the sooner we can relax.

266
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:23,720
Ten years ago, when you reported
Li Junsheng,

267
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:25,280
you warned Zhang Jinghang first.

268
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:27,360
That gave Zhang Jichuan time to escape.

269
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:28,640
So technically,

270
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:30,240
Zhang Jinghang shouldn't still hate you.

271
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:32,360
But there's one thing I don't get.

272
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:33,880
In every loop,

273
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:35,520
Li Junsheng is the one who runs me over.

274
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:38,600
Why is Li Junsheng doing
Zhang Jinghang's dirty work?

275
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:40,480
Ever since Li Junsheng got out,

276
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:41,400
he's been addicted to gambling

277
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:42,560
and buried in debt.

278
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:44,080
He even started taking jobs
on the dark web

279
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:46,200
to "solve problems" for people.

280
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:48,800
Maybe Zhang Jinghang didn't even know

281
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:50,120
the guy who accepted his job

282
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:51,920
was actually Li Junsheng.

283
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:22,240
(In Memoriam)

284
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:35,600
If Li Junsheng hadn't targeted me,

285
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:37,640
I could've stayed with you
a few more days

286
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:39,320
to help with your mom's funeral.

287
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:42,440
If we hadn't pinned everything
on Li Junsheng back then,

288
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:44,240
you never would've escaped the country.

289
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:46,320
Now that he knows you're back,

290
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:47,480
he won't let this go.

291
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:49,520
And...

292
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:51,800
once the police find out you're back,

293
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:54,160
with three people dead from those drugs,

294
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:56,280
you won't get off lightly.

295
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:58,840
Dad,

296
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:00,600
you need to go.

297
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:03,760
I've already booked a boat
to go out to sea.

298
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:05,960
I'll leave in a few days.

299
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:11,080
I'll come see you during break.

300
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:12,560
Okay.

301
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:16,880
The one who ran Li Junsheng over

302
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:18,840
must've been Zhang Jichuan.

303
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:32,200
So Zhang Jinghang

304
00:12:32,640 --> 00:12:34,560
knew about his father's crimes
all along.

305
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,200
He lied to us.

306
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:38,640
He's been covering for his dad
this whole time.

307
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:40,400
And now I'm starting to think

308
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:42,160
Li Junsheng didn't kidnap me
to get to you.

309
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:43,760
He was after Zhang Jinghang.

310
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:47,600
Li Junsheng probably used Zhang Jinghang

311
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:48,960
to lure Zhang Jichuan to the docks.

312
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:50,240
(One Week Earlier)

313
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:50,800
(Xiyu!)

314
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:52,640
(Xiyu!)

315
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:01,520
Li Junsheng!

316
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,000
Let my son go.

317
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:05,640
Dad!

318
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:06,520
Zhang Jichuan,

319
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:08,040
you finally showed up.

320
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:09,520
That day,

321
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:10,760
I happened to call the police
to save you.

322
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:13,960
Otherwise, how could it
be such a coincidence?

323
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,040
Zhang Jichuan had barely
boarded the boat

324
00:13:16,520 --> 00:13:17,440
when it went down in a storm.

325
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,120
No wonder he hates us so much.

326
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,400
Zhang Jinghang blames us

327
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:23,600
for his father's death.

328
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:27,720
If the police take them all down

329
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:29,040
and Zhang Jinghang gets arrested,

330
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:30,440
you won't be killed.

331
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:33,680
Then maybe we can finally
break the loop.

332
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:35,800
What's your idea?

333
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:12,200
♪I hide my racing heart without a sound♪

334
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:18,760
♪I close my eyes and pretend
the story's been reset♪

335
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:22,880
♪I steer clear of every path
that leads to you♪

336
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:26,040
♪Trying to outrun the storm
we're destined for♪

337
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:28,960
♪I thought if I didn't hear, see,
or speak of you♪

338
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:32,440
♪I could cut every thread
that ties us together♪

339
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:38,680
♪Through the endless night,
I guard my only secret♪

340
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:45,240
♪In this new cycle, I watch you
become innocent again♪

341
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:48,520
♪I tried to erase the fire we once had♪

342
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:52,400
♪But I can't erase your name
carved into my bones♪

343
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,240
♪The more I try to leave you behind♪

344
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:59,360
♪The deeper I sink with no end in sight♪

345
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:02,240
♪What if I stayed a little farther away♪

346
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:05,640
♪Could I finally break free
from this cycle♪

347
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:08,040
♪What if I took things a little slower♪

348
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:12,040
♪Could I delay the moment
everything falls apart♪

349
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:16,120
♪Maybe if I retreat to the edge
of my dreams♪

350
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:19,160
♪I could give you another future♪

351
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:25,600
♪A tomorrow where I no longer exist♪

352
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:27,920
♪Even if I never want to see you again♪

353
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,560
♪This nightmare still won't end♪

354
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:31,320
♪Even if it all plays out again♪

355
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:33,600
♪I'll still find my way back to you♪

356
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:37,600
♪Even if having you only leaves me
in your debt♪

357
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:41,560
♪It's still better than
losing you forever♪
